REASON main: C-SIGN gives s1, s2 > 0, so main(t) = I[FE0] (1 + s1 t + s2 t^2) increases in t; its t = 1/300 value bounds every J >= 300
REASON R3: t^3 and t^4 times untilted integrals of fixed polynomials (twlib hbar(j, a, aZ) has no t): nondecreasing in t
REASON R_cub: Q_t(t') >= Q_t(1/300) in the Loewner order for t' <= 1/300 (the t-part t cfun(a_v) of the tilt is PSD), the integrands X_T^4, H1^4, hhat^4 are >= 0, hhat(t') <= hhat(1/300) monomialwise, and t^3 grows: nondecreasing in t
REASON R_F: (t^3/6) E3(a) I_t[X_T^4], with I_t nondecreasing in t as for R_cub: nondecreasing in t
REASON tail: e^{-lam_v J a_v} decreases in J; T_v <= (1 - theta2)^{-d/2} I[1] is free of J (C-PROP, C-RANK); L2 is 1, t, t^2 times untilted integrals: nonincreasing in J
REASON far: C-FAR (p/J < c(a), c(aZ) for J >= 300), so J^p e^{-c J} decreases in J
REASON PR: PR = pref_arb(N), a ratio of reduced Laplacian determinants of fixed strip graphs, does not depend on J
REASON TW: every TW error sits inside the certified J = 300 enclosures; each reason compares exact J-bounds with the exact J = 300 bound, which the enclosure upper end majorizes
REASON Z4: each J-bound is twrig4's at its own Omega(J) and tilt T(1/J) before the comparison, so the comparison is between valid bounds, pointwise in J
CHECKS all PASS
